# Statistics Foundations – Business Analytics

## 🎯 Business Problem
Companies often rely on averages to understand performance. However, averages can be misleading when data contains extreme values.

This project explores how statistical measures affect business interpretation.

---

## 📊 Dataset
Simulated e-commerce transaction data.

Fields:
- order_value
- customer_id
- date

---

## 🧠 Methods

- Mean vs Median comparison
- Outlier detection
- Distribution analysis
- Basic descriptive statistics

---

## 📈 Key Insights

- Mean is highly sensitive to outliers
- Median better represents typical customer behavior
- A small number of large transactions can distort management reporting
- Distribution analysis is necessary before drawing business conclusions
- Similar averages can hide very different business realities
- Low variability improves forecasting and operational planning

---

## 💡 Business Impact

- Reporting should include median values
- Outliers must be analyzed separately
- Customer segmentation is more reliable than global averages

---

## 🛠 Tools

- Python (pandas)
- Jupyter Notebook

## Hypothesis

H0: The new version has no effect on conversion rate.
H1: The new version changes the conversion rate.

## Results

Group A Conversion Rate: 30%
Group B Conversion Rate: 70%
Observed Difference: +40 Percentage Points

## Key Insights

- Variant B achieved a higher conversion rate.
- The sample size is very small.
- Statistical significance should be evaluated before rollout.
- Business decisions should not rely solely on observed conversion differences.

## Recommendation

Variant B shows promising performance. However, due to the small sample size, 
additional testing with a larger user base is recommended before a full rollout decision.
